<title>KUWAIT: Kuwait bank assets rise in October-official.</title>
<headline>Kuwait bank assets rise in October-official.</headline>
<dateline>KUWAIT 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Combined assets of banks operating in Kuwait rose to 11.348 billion dinars at the end of October from 11.134 billion at the end of September, Central Bank said in a monthly bulletin.</p>
<p>Assets were 11.340 billion dinars in October 1995.</p>
<p>			Figures in million Kuwaiti dinars</p>
<p>					   October '96    October '95</p>
<p> Cash					  45.3		 46.3</p>
<p> Balances with Central Bank	     4.9		 17.9</p>
<p> Public debt instruments	    1,843.3	    1,896.7</p>
<p> Debt purchase bonds		  2,888.2	    3,644.4</p>
<p> Other local investments		292.0		319.6</p>
<p>Credit facilities to</p>
<p>  residents			     3,081.2	    2,221.4</p>
<p> Foreign assets			 2,157.2	    2,162.3</p>
<p> Inter bank local deposits	    561.2		542.4</p>
<p> Other assets			     474.4		489.1</p>
<p> Total				   11,347.6	   11,340.0</p>
<p>Note. Data covers eight commercial and specialised banks, the Islamic institution Kuwait Finance House and a Kuwaiti branch of a Bahrain-based bank.</p>
<p>Debt purchase bonds include the value of the purchase by the government of the real estate portfolio of Kuwait Finance House in December 1991.</p>
<p>Slight discrepancies in totals are due to rounding.</p>
<p>($1=0.303 dinar)</p>
<p>-- Kuwait newsroom +965-240-8945</p>
</text>
